          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy a 36 inch dust mop first and use it weekly; it does more for an epoxy floor than any cleaner. Add a microfiber flat mop with two pads for the monthly wet clean and a 24 inch squeegee matched to your floor, moss rubber for smooth coatings and foam for flake.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Keep acids, citrus, abrasive pads and soap off the floor, follow your coating's own care sheet for what goes in the bucket, and hang the tools by the door where you will actually use them. That is the whole kit, and it costs less than a single spot repair.
